    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34279" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pectŏrālis</span></b> , e,
			adj.
		pectus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the
			breast</i>, <i>breast-</i>, <i>pectoral</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pectorale os,</span>”
				<i>the breast-bone</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cels. 8,
					1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tunicula,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 14, 9, 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cinctum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 11, p. 261, 36</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fascia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Isa. 3, 24</span></i>
			 (Hier. in loc., <i><span class="en">Vulg. Jer. 2, 32</span></i>).—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pectŏrāle</span></b> , is,
				n., <i>a breast-plate</i>, <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 5, § 115</span></i>
			Müll.; <i><span class="en">Plin. 34, 7, 18, §
		43</span></i>.</div>
